## Requirement
# REQ-21 A negative promo percent means no discount

Operations sometimes enter -5 in the promo field to mean "no promotion".
Today applyDiscount() throws on it: the customer sees an error page at
checkout, and Order Import rejects the row.

- A negative percent counts as no discount: a 200-cent cart at -5% totals
  200 cents, and an imported 105-cent row at -5% totals 105 cents.
- Behaviour to preserve: percents from 0 to 100 give the same totals as before.

Affected workflows: Checkout, Order Import.


## Author's PR brief (claims by the author; not yet verified)
Author: Coding agent (authoring pass)
Why: REQ-21: operations enter -5 in the promo field to mean no promotion. applyDiscount() threw a RangeError on it, so checkout showed an error page and Order Import rejected the row.
Before: A 200-cent cart at -5% throws RangeError. Checkout fails.
After: A 200-cent cart at -5% totals 200 cents. A bad promo percent no longer fails checkout.
Behaviour to preserve: Percents from 0 to 100 give the same totals as before.
Approach: In applyDiscount(), replace the range check that threw with a floor at 0, so a negative percent means no discount. Whole-cent integer maths unchanged.
Alternatives considered: Validate the promo field in the admin screen instead. Rejected: Order Import files come from partners and would still fail.
Rollback: Revert the PR commit. No data migration.
Open gaps stated by author: None stated
Claims:
- applyDiscount() treats a negative percent as no discount instead of throwing.
- Checkout totals 200 cents for a 200-cent cart at -5%.
- Order Import totals 105 cents for a 105-cent row at -5%.
- Percents from 0 to 100 keep their Checkout totals.
- All tests pass.
- applyDiscount() has no callers other than Checkout and Order Import.

